# Line endings are NORMALISED IN THE INDEX and left to the platform in the working
# tree. Without this, whether a file is stored LF or CRLF depends on each
# contributor's global `core.autocrlf` — a setting nothing in this repository can
# see, and the Format lane's result depends on it: `ruff format --check` compares
# against what the installed formatter would produce, and the committed evidence
# artefact is reconciled byte-for-byte against a fresh run in CI. Both are
# currently green because `ruff` auto-detects line endings and every contributor
# so far has had `autocrlf=true`. Neither is a property anyone chose, which is why
# this file exists.
#
# `git add --renormalize .` was a no-op when this landed: the index already held
# LF throughout.
* text=auto
